{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"First fix attempt: re-centering an off-screen restored frame.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" Defaults held ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSWindow Frame rc-git.window = -1080 -40 1080 1355","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" — saved on an external display that sat left of the main screen and was later detached. A guard was added to re-center when the restored frame intersects no attached screen. Real defect, but secondary: the window still never appeared, because the code never got that far.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
